IMPORT prelude

-- Land Tax Management Act 1956 (NSW), read with the Land Tax Act 1956 (NSW) -- the seat-neutral core.
--
-- The rules are written in the Acts' own actors and terms: "the owner", "the joint owners", "the taxpayer", "the
-- foreign person", "the members of the family", "the Chief Commissioner". The individual owner's questions are in
-- ltma-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and restates no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Land Tax Management Act 1956: s 7; s 8; s 9(1)-(4); s 9AA(1), (2) and (6) (one adjustment, an
-- input), (7), (11); s 10(1)(r) and Schedule 1A cll 1-9 and 11-15; Schedule 2 cl 70; s 12(1A)-(1B); s 27(2)-(4) with
-- ss 33 and 34; s 39(1), (3); s 40; s 62P; s 62S. Land Tax Act 1956: s 3AL(1), (2)(a), (5); Schedule 13 Part 1;
-- s 5A(1)-(4); s 5B(1)-(4).
-- REGULATIVE RULES (DEONTIC): s 12(1A)-(1B) (the return); Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6) and cl 7(3A)-(4) (revocations);
-- Schedule 1A cl 12(3)-(5) (the family election); s 39(1), (3) (payment); s 40 (the early payment discount); Land Tax
-- Act s 5B(2)-(4) (the 200-day residence requirement).
--
-- EDITIONS. Land Tax Management Act 1956 No 26, NSW Legislation version 2024-12-02 (act-1956-026), and Land Tax Act 1956
-- No 27, version 2024-12-02 (act-1956-027), both from the Open Australian Legal Corpus as collected on 10 March 2025 and
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-1956-026.txt and
-- ../../../land-tax-act-1956/registers/source-bundle/act-1956-027.txt. NOT THE CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT AND MAY BE OUT OF
-- DATE. The thresholds are encoded as the deposited s 62P and s 62S state them; for the 2025 and later land tax years
-- they must be checked against the current register.
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025 (State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0),
-- as collected in the Open Australian Legal Corpus 7.1.0 (Umar Butt / Isaacus, CC BY 4.0). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
--
-- NOT COVERED (an explicit `not covered` answer): land subject to a special trust and land owned by a non-concessional
-- company (Schedule 13 Parts 2-4); anything that needs the Land Tax Management Regulation 2024 (not deposited); land tax
-- years before 2009; residential land of a foreign person partly used for other purposes (Duties Act s 104ZB).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. A land tax year is named by its calendar year (s 3(1): "a period of 12 months starting on 1 January").
-- Money is in Australian dollars. A share or a rate is a fraction (one half is 0.5). In the regulative rules the clock
-- counts days from the day each rule names.

§ `Land Tax Management Act 1956 and Land Tax Act 1956 (NSW) -- the core`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A rule that can reach a gap answers `not covered`, with one of these reasons.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- Land Tax Act s 3AL(2)(b), Schedule 13 Part 2
    `land subject to a special trust is taxed at the Schedule 13 Part 2 rate, which is not encoded`
    -- Land Tax Act s 3AL(2)(c)-(d), Schedule 13 Parts 3 and 4; Management Act s 29
    `land owned by a non-concessional company is taxed at the Schedule 13 Part 3 or 4 rate, which is not encoded`
    -- Management Act s 3(1) "owner" (c); Land Tax Act s 5A(4)(i), s 5BA(1)
    `the answer depends on the Land Tax Management Regulation 2024, which is not deposited`
    -- Land Tax Act Schedules 1-12 (earlier rates, not encoded); Management Act s 62S starts with 2009
    `the encoding has no rate scale or premium rate threshold for a land tax year before 2009`
    -- Land Tax Act s 5A(4)(d), Duties Act 1997 s 104ZB (not deposited here)
    `residential land partly used for other purposes needs the Duties Act 1997 s 104ZB apportionment factor, not deposited`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Arithmetic and the calendar`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a leap year` MEANS
       (`the year` MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (`the year` MODULO 100 EQUALS 0)))
    OR `the year` MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days in month` MEANS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `the year` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `the month` EQUALS 4 OR `the month` EQUALS 6 OR `the month` EQUALS 9 OR `the month` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- A day some months later: the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month (31 August plus 6 months is
-- 28 or 29 February). READING: the Acts do not say how a period of months ends; this follows the usual calendar rule.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the lesser of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) `and` (`days in month` `the new month` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `months counted` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12 PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new year` MEANS FLOOR (`months counted` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month` MEANS (`months counted` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` MEANS `months after` `the day` (`n` TIMES 12)

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` `the first` `to` `the second` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or before` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

§§ `ss 7 and 8 -- what is taxed, and the day ownership is fixed`

-- s 7: "Land tax at such rates as may be fixed by any Act is to be levied and paid on the taxable value of all land
-- situated in New South Wales which is owned by taxpayers (other than land which is exempt from taxation under this
-- Act)." The rates are fixed by the Land Tax Act 1956 (s 3AL and Schedule 13, below).
-- s 8: "Land tax shall be charged on land as owned at midnight on the thirty-first day of December immediately preceding
-- the year for which the land tax is levied." Schedule 1A cl 1(1): "taxing date -- means midnight on the thirty-first day
-- of December."
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the taxing date for` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 (`the land tax year` MINUS 1)

-- Schedule 1A cl 7(3A): "the next taxing date immediately following the relevant taxing date".
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the next taxing date after the one for` MEANS `the taxing date for` (`the land tax year` PLUS 1)

§§ `ss 9 and 9AA -- taxable value and average value`

-- s 9(4): "The land value of land, in relation to a land tax year, is the value entered in the Register as the land value
-- of the land as at 1 July in the previous year." The land values are INPUTS: they come from the Valuer-General's
-- Register of Land Values, not from this Act.
-- s 9AA(1): the average value is "the average of the land value of the land in relation to the year for which the average
-- value is being ascertained (the current land tax year) and the land value of the land in relation to the 2 preceding
-- land tax years".
-- s 9AA(7): if the parcel "did not exist on 31 December immediately before either or both of the preceding land tax
-- years", the average is "(a) if the parcel did exist on 31 December immediately before one of the preceding land tax
-- years -- the average of the land value of the land in relation to the current land tax year and the land value of the
-- land in relation to the preceding land tax year immediately before which it did exist, or (b) in any other case -- the
-- land value of the land in relation to the current land tax year".
-- s 9AA(2), (6): a land value adjustment (a reduction the Act requires, or a special allowance under the Valuation of
-- Land Act 1916) is applied to the average value. It is ONE INPUT here; the reductions themselves (ss 9A-9E, 10(2)-(2C))
-- are not encoded. s 9AA(11): "If the average value of a parcel of land, after applying a land value adjustment, is less
-- than zero, the average value of the parcel is taken to be zero."
DECLARE `Parcel land values` HAS
    `land value for the current land tax year`                                IS A NUMBER
    `land value for the preceding land tax year`                              IS A NUMBER
    `land value for the land tax year before that`                            IS A NUMBER
    `preceding land tax years before whose 31 December the parcel existed`    IS A NUMBER
    `land value adjustment`                                                   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A `Parcel land values`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average value of` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`the unadjusted average` MINUS `the parcel`'s `land value adjustment`) `and` 0
    WHERE
        `the unadjusted average` MEANS
            IF `the parcel`'s `preceding land tax years before whose 31 December the parcel existed` AT LEAST 2
            THEN (`the parcel`'s `land value for the current land tax year` PLUS `the parcel`'s `land value for the preceding land tax year` PLUS `the parcel`'s `land value for the land tax year before that`) DIVIDED BY 3
            ELSE IF `the parcel`'s `preceding land tax years before whose 31 December the parcel existed` EQUALS 1
                 THEN (`the parcel`'s `land value for the current land tax year` PLUS `the parcel`'s `land value for the preceding land tax year`) DIVIDED BY 2
                 ELSE `the parcel`'s `land value for the current land tax year`

§§ `Part 7 Division 4 -- the thresholds (ss 62P, 62S)`

-- s 62P, as deposited: 2006 $352,000 ... 2023 $969,000; "(s) for a land tax year after the 2023 land tax year --
-- $1,075,000". Schedule 2 cl 69(1): "An amount set out in section 62P for a land tax year is taken to be the tax threshold
-- for the land tax year." The text deposited is as at 2 December 2024: CHECK THE CURRENT REGISTER for 2025 and later.
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 62P tax threshold for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land tax year`
    WHEN 2006 THEN JUST 352000
    WHEN 2007 THEN JUST 352000
    WHEN 2008 THEN JUST 359000
    WHEN 2009 THEN JUST 368000
    WHEN 2010 THEN JUST 376000
    WHEN 2011 THEN JUST 387000
    WHEN 2012 THEN JUST 396000
    WHEN 2013 THEN JUST 406000
    WHEN 2014 THEN JUST 412000
    WHEN 2015 THEN JUST 432000
    WHEN 2016 THEN JUST 482000
    WHEN 2017 THEN JUST 549000
    WHEN 2018 THEN JUST 629000
    WHEN 2019 THEN JUST 692000
    WHEN 2020 THEN JUST 734000
    WHEN 2021 THEN JUST 755000
    WHEN 2022 THEN JUST 822000
    WHEN 2023 THEN JUST 969000
    OTHERWISE IF `the land tax year` GREATER THAN 2023 THEN JUST 1075000 ELSE NOTHING

-- s 62S, as deposited: 2009 $2,250,000 ... 2023 $5,925,000; "(p) for a land tax year after the 2023 land tax year --
-- $6,571,000". Schedule 2 cl 69(2) validates the amounts.
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the s 62S premium rate threshold for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land tax year`
    WHEN 2009 THEN JUST 2250000
    WHEN 2010 THEN JUST 2299000
    WHEN 2011 THEN JUST 2366000
    WHEN 2012 THEN JUST 2421000
    WHEN 2013 THEN JUST 2482000
    WHEN 2014 THEN JUST 2519000
    WHEN 2015 THEN JUST 2641000
    WHEN 2016 THEN JUST 2947000
    WHEN 2017 THEN JUST 3357000
    WHEN 2018 THEN JUST 3846000
    WHEN 2019 THEN JUST 4231000
    WHEN 2020 THEN JUST 4488000
    WHEN 2021 THEN JUST 4616000
    WHEN 2022 THEN JUST 5026000
    WHEN 2023 THEN JUST 5925000
    OTHERWISE IF `the land tax year` GREATER THAN 2023 THEN JUST 6571000 ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Thresholds` HAS
    `tax threshold`          IS A NUMBER
    `premium rate threshold` IS A NUMBER

-- Land Tax Act s 2A: "tax threshold" and "premium rate threshold" are as determined under the Principal Act, Part 7,
-- Division 4. Schedule 13 applies from the 2009 land tax year, the first with both thresholds.
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Thresholds`
`the thresholds for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 62P tax threshold for` `the land tax year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered` `the encoding has no rate scale or premium rate threshold for a land tax year before 2009`
    WHEN JUST `the tax threshold` THEN
        CONSIDER `the s 62S premium rate threshold for` `the land tax year`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `not covered` `the encoding has no rate scale or premium rate threshold for a land tax year before 2009`
        WHEN JUST `the premium threshold` THEN
            `answered` (`Thresholds` WITH `tax threshold` IS `the tax threshold`, `premium rate threshold` IS `the premium threshold`)

§§ `Land Tax Act s 3AL and Schedule 13 Part 1 -- the general rate`

-- Schedule 13 Part 1 (General rate (where tax threshold applies)):
--   "is not more than the tax threshold -- nil";
--   "is more than the tax threshold but not more than the premium rate threshold -- $100 plus 1.6 per cent of the amount
--   by which the taxable value exceeds the tax threshold";
--   "is more than the premium rate threshold -- $100 plus (a) 1.6 per cent of the amount by which premium rate threshold
--   exceeds the tax threshold, and (b) 2 per cent of the amount by which the taxable value exceeds the premium rate
--   threshold".
-- s 3AL(2)(a): Part 1 is the applicable rate except for land subject to a special trust or owned by a non-concessional
-- company (not covered). No rounding is stated; none is applied.
GIVEN `the taxable value` IS A NUMBER, `the thresholds` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 13 Part 1 land tax on` MEANS
    IF `the taxable value` AT MOST `the thresholds`'s `tax threshold`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the taxable value` AT MOST `the thresholds`'s `premium rate threshold`
         THEN 100 PLUS (1.6% TIMES (`the taxable value` MINUS `the thresholds`'s `tax threshold`))
         ELSE 100 PLUS (1.6% TIMES (`the thresholds`'s `premium rate threshold` MINUS `the thresholds`'s `tax threshold`)) PLUS (2% TIMES (`the taxable value` MINUS `the thresholds`'s `premium rate threshold`))

-- s 3AL(5): "If the total amount of land tax payable pursuant to this section by any person in any year would, but for
-- this subsection, be less than $100, no land tax is payable." READING (NOTES.md finding 4): applied to the amount each
-- assessment leaves payable, after the s 27(4) deduction.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`after the s 3AL(5) minimum` MEANS
    IF `the amount` LESS THAN 100 THEN 0 ELSE `the amount`

§§ `ss 9 and 27 -- the owner's assessments, alone and jointly`

-- s 9(1)-(2): "Land tax is payable by the owner of land on the taxable value of all the land owned by that owner which is
-- not exempt from taxation under this Act. ... The taxable value of that land is the total sum of the average value of
-- each parcel of that land."
-- s 27(2): joint owners "are to be jointly assessed and liable in respect of the aggregate value of their proportionate
-- interests in the land as if the land were owned by one person ... without taking into account any land owned by any one
-- of them in severalty or as joint owner with any other person".
-- s 27(3): "Each joint owner of land shall in addition be separately assessed and liable in respect of (a) his or her
-- individual interest in the land ..., together with (b) any other land owned by him or her in severalty, and (c) his or
-- her individual interests in any other land."
-- s 27(4): "The joint owners in respect of their joint assessment shall be deemed to be the primary taxpayer, and each
-- joint owner in respect of his or her separate assessment to be a secondary taxpayer; and from the land tax payable in
-- respect of his or her interest in the land by each joint owner under subsection (3) there shall be deducted such amount
-- (if any) as is necessary to prevent double taxation."
-- s 33: the deduction is the lesser of "(i) the amount of land tax payable in respect of the land or interest by the
-- secondary taxpayer, or (ii) the amount of land tax (if any) payable in respect of the land or interest by the primary
-- taxpayer".
-- s 34(1): the tax payable "in respect of any land or interest" is the whole tax in "the proportion which the average
-- value of the land or interest referred to bears to the average value of all the land ... owned by the person".
--
-- One joint holding is the land one group of joint owners owns together, with the owner's share of it. INPUT LIMIT: no
-- joint owner is exempt (s 27(2) "excluding the proportionate value of the interest of any joint owner so exempt" is not
-- encoded), and every value is of land that is not exempt.
DECLARE `Joint holding` HAS
    `average value of the land held jointly` IS A NUMBER
    `the owner's share`                      IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Land owned at the taxing date` HAS
    `land tax year`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `average value of non-exempt land owned in severalty`    IS A NUMBER
    `joint holdings`                                         IS A LIST OF `Joint holding`
    `some of the land is subject to a special trust`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a non-concessional company is an owner of some of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner owns land only as a prescribed lessee`        IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Land tax assessed` HAS
    `taxable value on the separate assessment`  IS A NUMBER
    `payable on the separate assessment`        IS A NUMBER
    `payable on the joint assessments`          IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the holding` IS A `Joint holding`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the owner's interest in` MEANS
    `the holding`'s `the owner's share` TIMES `the holding`'s `average value of the land held jointly`

GIVEN `the land` IS A `Land owned at the taxing date`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the separate taxable value of` MEANS
    `the land`'s `average value of non-exempt land owned in severalty` PLUS sum (map `the value of the owner's interest in` (`the land`'s `joint holdings`))

-- s 27(2): the joint assessment, the joint owners being the primary taxpayer.
GIVEN `the holding` IS A `Joint holding`, `the thresholds` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the joint assessment on` MEANS
    `after the s 3AL(5) minimum` (`the Schedule 13 Part 1 land tax on` (`the holding`'s `average value of the land held jointly`) `the thresholds`)

-- s 27(4), ss 33 and 34: the deduction from the separate assessment for one joint interest.
GIVEN `the holding` IS A `Joint holding`, `the separate taxable value` IS A NUMBER, `the separate tax` IS A NUMBER, `the thresholds` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 27(4) deduction for` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `the secondary taxpayer's tax on the interest` `and` `the primary taxpayer's tax on the interest`
    WHERE
        `the secondary taxpayer's tax on the interest` MEANS
            IF `the separate taxable value` EQUALS 0
            THEN 0
            ELSE `the separate tax` TIMES (`the value of the owner's interest in` `the holding`) DIVIDED BY `the separate taxable value`
        `the primary taxpayer's tax on the interest` MEANS
            `the joint assessment on` `the holding` `the thresholds` TIMES `the holding`'s `the owner's share`

GIVEN `the land` IS A `Land owned at the taxing date`, `the thresholds` IS A `Thresholds`
GIVETH A `Land tax assessed`
`the assessments of` MEANS
    `Land tax assessed` WITH
        `taxable value on the separate assessment` IS `the separate taxable value`
        `payable on the separate assessment`       IS `after the s 3AL(5) minimum` (`the separate tax` MINUS `the deductions`)
        `payable on the joint assessments`         IS sum (map (GIVEN `h` YIELD `the joint assessment on` `h` `the thresholds`) (`the land`'s `joint holdings`))
    WHERE
        `the separate taxable value` MEANS `the separate taxable value of` `the land`
        `the separate tax` MEANS `the Schedule 13 Part 1 land tax on` `the separate taxable value` `the thresholds`
        `the deductions` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN `h` YIELD `the s 27(4) deduction for` `h` `the separate taxable value` `the separate tax` `the thresholds`) (`the land`'s `joint holdings`))

-- The whole computation, with the cases the encoding does not cover.
-- s 3 "Owner" (c): "in relation to any leasehold estate in land ... a person ... prescribed for the purposes of this
-- paragraph" -- prescribed by the regulations, which are not deposited.
GIVEN `the land` IS A `Land owned at the taxing date`
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Land tax assessed`
`the land tax assessed on` MEANS
    IF `the land`'s `some of the land is subject to a special trust`
    THEN `not covered` `land subject to a special trust is taxed at the Schedule 13 Part 2 rate, which is not encoded`
    ELSE IF `the land`'s `a non-concessional company is an owner of some of the land`
         THEN `not covered` `land owned by a non-concessional company is taxed at the Schedule 13 Part 3 or 4 rate, which is not encoded`
         ELSE IF `the land`'s `the owner owns land only as a prescribed lessee`
              THEN `not covered` `the answer depends on the Land Tax Management Regulation 2024, which is not deposited`
              ELSE CONSIDER `the thresholds for` (`the land`'s `land tax year`)
                   WHEN `answered` `the thresholds` THEN `answered` (`the assessments of` `the land` `the thresholds`)
                   WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`

§§ `s 10(1)(r) and Schedule 1A -- the principal place of residence exemption`

-- s 10(1)(r): exempt is "land that is exempt from taxation under the principal place of residence exemption, as provided
-- for by Schedule 1A". One case is one parcel (or one set of lots used as one home) on one taxing date.
--
-- Schedule 1A cl 2(1): "Land used and occupied by the owner as the principal place of residence of the owner of the land,
-- and for no other purpose, is exempt ... if the land is (a) a parcel of residential land, or (b) a strata lot or,
-- subject to this Schedule, land comprised of 2 or more strata lots."
-- cl 1(2): "a reference to the owner of land includes, if there are joint owners, any one or more of those joint owners."
-- cl 2(3): "If the owner of land is entitled to the exemption ..., no other person is liable to be assessed for taxation
-- under this Act in respect of the land" -- so an exempt home is left out of every co-owner's taxable value.

-- cl 3(1): "residential land means land that is used and occupied for residential purposes and for no other purpose, that
-- use and occupation being use and occupation of a building or buildings designed, constructed or adapted for residential
-- purposes, other than a building or buildings -- (a) comprised of strata lots or residential units, or (b) containing
-- (out of the total of all rooms in the building or buildings) occupancies other than that of the owner, or (c) from any
-- part of which income is derived."
-- cl 4: one "excluded residential occupancy" may be disregarded "even if income is derived from" it: "(a) one room, (b)
-- one suite of rooms (not being a flat) ..., (c) one flat, (d) one suite of rooms ... and one room, (e) one flat and one
-- room, (f) 2 rooms, each of which is separately occupied"; cl 4(4): on 2 or more lots, it "must be located on a lot or
-- strata lot that is also used and occupied by the owner of the land for residential purposes".
-- cl 5(1): "not more than one room is used primarily for business purposes, the use of the land for the purpose of the
-- business may be disregarded if the business is primarily conducted elsewhere."
-- cl 13 (lots other than strata lots) and cl 14 (strata lots): 2 or more lots are exempt only if they adjoin, are "in the
-- same ownership", and are the site of (or comprise) "a single residence"; cl 13(2) and cl 14(2) say when lots adjoin and
-- form one residence. Those tests are FACTS here.
DECLARE `The land and its use` HAS
    `is a strata lot or strata lots`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building is designed, constructed or adapted for residential purposes`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of lots`                                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the lots adjoin`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lots are in the same ownership`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lots are a single residence`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a residential occupancy other than the owner's`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `that occupancy is one excluded residential occupancy`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `that occupancy is on a lot the owner also lives on`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `one room is used primarily for a business conducted primarily elsewhere`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land is used for another purpose or earns other income`                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 2(2): "Land is not used and occupied as the principal place of residence of a person unless (a) the land, and no
-- other land, has been continuously used and occupied by the person for residential purposes and for no other purposes
-- since 1 July in the year preceding the tax year in which land tax is levied, or (b) in any other case, the Chief
-- Commissioner is satisfied that the land is used and occupied by the person as the person's principal place of
-- residence." (b) is answered conditionally: an input.
--
-- cl 6, the owner building a home on unoccupied land:
-- (1) the owner "intends to use and occupy the land solely as the owner's principal place of residence";
-- (2) "(a) the land is unoccupied because the owner intends to carry out, or is carrying out, building or other works
-- necessary to facilitate the owner's intended use and occupation of the land as a principal place of residence, and (b)
-- if those building or other works have physically commenced on the land, no income has been derived from the use and
-- occupation of the land since that commencement, and (c) the intended use and occupation of the land is not unlawful";
-- (3) only in "(a) 4 tax years immediately following the year in which the person became owner of the land, or (b) if,
-- after the person became owner and before the building or other works physically commence, the land is used and occupied
-- for residential purposes by another person -- 4 tax years immediately following the tax year in which the other person
-- ceases to use and occupy the land for those purposes";
-- (4)(a): in a (3)(b) period, only if "the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that, by the end of the first of the 4 tax
-- years concerned (i) the building or other works will be, or have been, physically commenced, or (ii) significant steps
-- will be, or have been, taken" (an input);
-- (7): not if "(a) the person or any member of the person's family ... is entitled to have the person's or member's actual
-- use and occupation of other land taken into account under section 9C or 9D or under this Schedule, or (b) the person
-- owns land outside New South Wales that is the principal place of residence of the person or a member of the person's
-- family ..., or (c) the land, or the land if combined with any adjoining land of which the person is an owner, is
-- capable of having more than 2 residences or residential units lawfully built on it";
-- (7A): the Chief Commissioner "may extend the period of 4 tax years ... to a period of up to 6 tax years" (an input);
-- (8): "unoccupied land means land that is not being used or occupied for any purpose".
DECLARE `Building facts` HAS
    `the land is unoccupied`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner intends to live there solely as principal place of residence`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is unoccupied because the owner intends to carry out or is carrying out the works` IS A BOOLEAN
    `income has been derived since the works physically began`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the intended use is unlawful`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the year the owner became the owner`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `another person lived there after the purchase and before the works began`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the year that person stopped living there`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the works began or significant steps were taken by the end of the first year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period in tax years, as the Chief Commissioner has extended it`             IS A NUMBER
    `the owner or a family member has other land counted as a principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner owns land outside NSW that is the principal place of residence of the owner or a family member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land could lawfully have more than 2 residences built on it`                IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 7, a change of principal place of residence. (1): on the relevant taxing date "(a) a person is the owner of land
-- (the former residence) that was the principal place of residence of the person on the relevant taxing date or was the
-- principal place of residence of the person on the preceding taxing date, and (b) the person is the owner of other land
-- (the new residence) that is being or is intended to be used and occupied by the person as the person's principal
-- place of residence", then both are taken to be the person's principal place of residence on that taxing date.
-- (2) only if "(a) the former residence has not been used or occupied except as the person's principal place of
-- residence, and no income has been derived from the use or occupation of the residence, since the preceding 1 July,
-- except -- (i) income derived from an excluded residential occupancy ..., or (ii) income derived under a lease or licence
-- entered into by the purchaser under a contract for the sale of the former residence for a period pending completion of
-- the sale, and (b) the person became the owner of the new residence within the period of 6 months before the relevant
-- taxing date, and (c) since the person became owner of the new residence the new residence has not been used or occupied
-- except -- (i) as the person's principal place of residence, or (ii) by a tenant under a lease entered into by the
-- previous owner." (3): not "for more than one taxing date".
DECLARE `Moving facts` HAS
    `the owner owns both a former residence and a new residence`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the former residence was the owner's principal place of residence on this or the preceding taxing date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the new residence is being or is intended to be the owner's principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the former residence was used only as the owner's home, without other income, since the preceding 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the owner became the owner of the new residence`                        IS A DATE
    `the new residence was used only as the owner's home or by a tenant of the previous owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `both residences were already exempt under clause 7 on an earlier taxing date`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 8, absence from a former residence. (1) the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that "(a) the person used and occupied the
-- former residence as a principal place of residence for a continuous period of at least 6 months, and (b) the person
-- does not own any other land used and occupied by the person as a principal place of residence";
-- (2) "The maximum period ... is 6 years starting at the end of the last period (of at least 6 months) during which the
-- former residence was used and occupied by the person as a principal place of residence";
-- (3A) it ceases "if the land ceases to be capable of being used and occupied as a residence and remains incapable of
-- being so used and occupied for a period exceeding 4 years";
-- (4) "Any period during which a person is in full time care is not to be counted toward the maximum period"; (5) full time
-- care: "(a) resides at a hospital or mental hospital as a patient of the hospital, or (b) resides at an aged care
-- establishment ... while being provided with residential care, or respite care, or (c) resides with another person (a
-- carer) who is eligible for a carer payment under the Social Security Act 1991 of the Commonwealth because the carer
-- provides care to the person";
-- (6) only if "no income has been derived from the use or occupation of the former residence in the preceding tax year,
-- except as permitted by subclause (7)"; (7) "(a) ... the period for which any such right of occupation is conferred does
-- not exceed a continuous period of 6 months, or a total period of 182 days, in the tax year, or (b) ... the income is no
-- more than is reasonably required to cover council, water and energy rates and charges and maintenance costs"; (7A)
-- "each overnight stay counts as one day". READING (finding 6): (7)(a) is met only if neither limit is exceeded.
DECLARE `Absence facts` HAS
    `the owner lived there as principal place of residence continuously for at least 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner owns other land the owner lives in as principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the owner stopped living there`                                         IS A DATE
    `days in full time care since then`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `income was derived from the land in the preceding tax year`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a right of occupation in that year ran continuously for more than 6 months`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of occupation let in that year`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the income was no more than rates, charges and maintenance costs`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land has been incapable of being used as a residence for more than 4 years` IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 9: "(1) If, immediately before the death of a person, the person was an owner of land and used and occupied the land
-- as the person's principal place of residence, liability for land tax in respect of the land is to be assessed as if
-- the person had not died and had continued to so use and occupy the land. (2) Subclause (1) operates only until
-- whichever of the following happens first -- (a) a period of 2 years expires after the date of the deceased person's
-- death, (b) the land is transferred to any person (other than the deceased person's personal representative, or a
-- beneficiary of the deceased person's estate)." (3)-(4): the Chief Commissioner may extend the 2 years, in writing (an
-- input).
DECLARE `Death facts` HAS
    `immediately before death the owner owned the land and lived there as principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the owner died`                                                         IS A DATE
    `the land has been transferred to someone other than the personal representative or a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Chief Commissioner has extended the 2 years in writing`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the extended period ends`                                               IS A DATE

DECLARE `Use at the taxing date` IS ONE OF
    `the owner lives there` HAS
        `continuously since 1 July, in that land and no other`                       IS A BOOLEAN
        `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is the owner's principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner is building a home there` HAS `the building facts` IS A `Building facts`
    `the owner is moving home`           HAS `the moving facts`   IS A `Moving facts`
    `the owner is away`                  HAS `the absence facts`  IS A `Absence facts`
    `the owner has died`                 HAS `the death facts`    IS A `Death facts`
    `none of these`

-- cl 11(1): not exempt if "(a) the land is owned, or jointly owned, by a company, unless the land is owned or jointly owned
-- by a trustee company acting in its representative capacity or a company acting in its capacity as trustee of a
-- concessional trust, or (b) the owner of the land, or each of the joint owners, who use and occupy the land as a principal
-- place of residence is an owner only by reason of being a trustee, or (c) the land is owned, or jointly owned, by a person
-- who is a trustee acting in the person's capacity as trustee of a special trust."
-- cl 12: "(1) ... only one place of residence may be treated as the principal place of residence of all members of the
-- same family. (2) If members of a family own ... more than one residence used and occupied by any of them as a principal
-- place of residence, the Chief Commissioner is to treat the one place of residence elected ... (5) If an election is not
-- made, the Chief Commissioner is to treat the residence that has the highest land value". (6): a family is "(a) a person
-- and the person's spouse (if any), (b) any dependent child or dependent step-child ... who ordinarily resides with the
-- person or the person's spouse"; (9) a dependent child is under 18 and not legally married. (10): clause 12 does not
-- prevent two residences under clause 7.
-- cl 15: "(1) A person is not entitled to a principal place of residence exemption in relation to land unless all the
-- persons who use and occupy the land as a principal place of residence together own at least a 25% interest in the land.
-- (2) This clause does not apply to a home buyer who is a participant in a shared equity scheme that is approved by the
-- Chief Commissioner under the Duties Act 1997, section 281." Schedule 2 cl 70: "(1) Schedule 1A, clause 15 does not
-- prevent a person from being entitled to a principal place of residence exemption in relation to land if the person
-- was previously entitled to the exemption in relation to the land. (2) This clause ceases to apply at the end of 31
-- December 2025." READING (finding 7): cl 70 is applied up to the 2025 land tax year.
DECLARE `Home at the taxing date` HAS
    `land tax year`                                                                  IS A NUMBER
    `the land`                                                                       IS A `The land and its use`
    `the use`                                                                        IS A `Use at the taxing date`
    `a company owns or co-owns it, other than a trustee company or a trustee of a concessional trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owners who live there are owners only as trustees`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns it`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the family owns another residence one of them uses as a principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the family lodged an election in time`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the family elected this residence`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `this residence has the highest land value of the family's residences`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage owned by the owners who live there`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `the owner is a participant in an approved shared equity scheme`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner was previously entitled to the exemption for this land`               IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Why not exempt` IS ONE OF
    `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
    `it is not a parcel of residential land or a strata lot`
    `it is 2 or more lots that do not meet clause 13 or 14`
    `clause 11 excludes land owned by a company or a trustee`
    `another residence is the family's principal place of residence under clause 12`
    `the owners who live there own less than a 25 percent interest`

DECLARE `Exemption answer` IS ONE OF
    `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
    `not exempt` HAS `the reason` IS A `Why not exempt`

-- cl 6(3), (7A): the clause 6 period runs from the year after the owner became the owner or, in a (3)(b) case, the year
-- after the other person stopped living there; it is 4 tax years, or up to 6 if the Chief Commissioner extends it.
GIVEN `the building facts` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the clause 6 period starts after` MEANS
    IF `the building facts`'s `another person lived there after the purchase and before the works began`
    THEN `the building facts`'s `the year that person stopped living there`
    ELSE `the building facts`'s `the year the owner became the owner`

GIVEN `the building facts` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the clause 6 period in tax years` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the greater of` (`the building facts`'s `the period in tax years, as the Chief Commissioner has extended it`) `and` 4) `and` 6

GIVEN `the building facts` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last tax year of the clause 6 period` MEANS
    `the year the clause 6 period starts after` `the building facts` PLUS `the clause 6 period in tax years` `the building facts`

-- cl 6(5): the period ends at the end of its last tax year.
GIVEN `the building facts` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the clause 6 period` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 (`the last tax year of the clause 6 period` `the building facts`)

GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER, `the building facts` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 6 applies` MEANS
        `the building facts`'s `the land is unoccupied`
    AND `the building facts`'s `the owner intends to live there solely as principal place of residence`
    AND `the building facts`'s `it is unoccupied because the owner intends to carry out or is carrying out the works`
    AND (NOT (`the building facts`'s `income has been derived since the works physically began`))
    AND (NOT (`the building facts`'s `the intended use is unlawful`))
    AND `the land tax year` GREATER THAN `the year the clause 6 period starts after` `the building facts`
    AND `the land tax year` AT MOST `the last tax year of the clause 6 period` `the building facts`
    AND (    (NOT (`the building facts`'s `another person lived there after the purchase and before the works began`))
          OR `the building facts`'s `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the works began or significant steps were taken by the end of the first year`)
    AND (NOT (`the building facts`'s `the owner or a family member has other land counted as a principal place of residence`))
    AND (NOT (`the building facts`'s `the owner owns land outside NSW that is the principal place of residence of the owner or a family member`))
    AND (NOT (`the building facts`'s `the land could lawfully have more than 2 residences built on it`))

-- cl 7(2)(b): "within the period of 6 months before the relevant taxing date". READING: on or after 1 July of the year
-- the taxing date falls in (6 months before midnight on 31 December), and not after the taxing date.
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER, `the moving facts` IS A `Moving facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 7 applies` MEANS
        `the moving facts`'s `the owner owns both a former residence and a new residence`
    AND `the moving facts`'s `the former residence was the owner's principal place of residence on this or the preceding taxing date`
    AND `the moving facts`'s `the new residence is being or is intended to be the owner's principal place of residence`
    AND `the moving facts`'s `the former residence was used only as the owner's home, without other income, since the preceding 1 July`
    AND `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 (`the land tax year` MINUS 1)) (`the moving facts`'s `the day the owner became the owner of the new residence`)
    AND `is on or before` (`the moving facts`'s `the day the owner became the owner of the new residence`) (`the taxing date for` `the land tax year`)
    AND `the moving facts`'s `the new residence was used only as the owner's home or by a tenant of the previous owner`
    AND (NOT (`the moving facts`'s `both residences were already exempt under clause 7 on an earlier taxing date`))

-- cl 8(2), (4): the last day the owner can be taken to live there -- 6 years from leaving, plus the days in full time care.
GIVEN `the absence facts` IS A `Absence facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the clause 8 period` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (`years after` (`the absence facts`'s `the day the owner stopped living there`) 6) PLUS `the absence facts`'s `days in full time care since then`)

GIVEN `the absence facts` IS A `Absence facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the clause 8(6)-(7) income test is met` MEANS
       (NOT (`the absence facts`'s `income was derived from the land in the preceding tax year`))
    OR (     (NOT (`the absence facts`'s `a right of occupation in that year ran continuously for more than 6 months`))
         AND `the absence facts`'s `days of occupation let in that year` AT MOST 182)
    OR `the absence facts`'s `the income was no more than rates, charges and maintenance costs`

GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER, `the absence facts` IS A `Absence facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 8 applies` MEANS
        `the absence facts`'s `the owner lived there as principal place of residence continuously for at least 6 months`
    AND (NOT (`the absence facts`'s `the owner owns other land the owner lives in as principal place of residence`))
    AND `is on or before` (`the absence facts`'s `the day the owner stopped living there`) (`the taxing date for` `the land tax year`)
    AND `is on or before` (`the taxing date for` `the land tax year`) (`the end of the clause 8 period` `the absence facts`)
    AND `the clause 8(6)-(7) income test is met` `the absence facts`
    AND (NOT (`the absence facts`'s `the land has been incapable of being used as a residence for more than 4 years`))

GIVEN `the death facts` IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the clause 9 period` MEANS
    IF `the death facts`'s `the Chief Commissioner has extended the 2 years in writing`
    THEN `the death facts`'s `the day the extended period ends`
    ELSE `years after` (`the death facts`'s `the day the owner died`) 2

GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER, `the death facts` IS A `Death facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 9 applies` MEANS
        `the death facts`'s `immediately before death the owner owned the land and lived there as principal place of residence`
    AND `is on or before` (`the death facts`'s `the day the owner died`) (`the taxing date for` `the land tax year`)
    AND `is on or before` (`the taxing date for` `the land tax year`) (`the end of the clause 9 period` `the death facts`)
    AND (NOT (`the death facts`'s `the land has been transferred to someone other than the personal representative or a beneficiary`))

-- cl 2(1)-(2) with cll 6 to 9: is the land used and occupied by the owner as principal place of residence, actually or
-- under a concession?
GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home at the taxing date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is used and occupied as the owner's principal place of residence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the home`'s `the use`
    WHEN `the owner lives there` `continuously` `satisfied` THEN `continuously` OR `satisfied`
    WHEN `the owner is building a home there` `b` THEN `clause 6 applies` (`the home`'s `land tax year`) `b`
    WHEN `the owner is moving home` `m` THEN `clause 7 applies` (`the home`'s `land tax year`) `m`
    WHEN `the owner is away` `a` THEN `clause 8 applies` (`the home`'s `land tax year`) `a`
    WHEN `the owner has died` `d` THEN `clause 9 applies` (`the home`'s `land tax year`) `d`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE

-- cl 2(1)(a)-(b), cl 3, cl 4, cl 5. READING (finding 5): for land the owner actually lives in, the use and income tests of
-- clauses 3 to 5 apply; under clauses 7, 8 and 9 the land must still be a residential building or a strata lot, but the
-- concession's own use and income conditions take the place of clauses 3 to 5; clause 6 land is unoccupied land.
GIVEN `the land` IS A `The land and its use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a residential building or a strata lot` MEANS
    `the land`'s `is a strata lot or strata lots` OR `the land`'s `the building is designed, constructed or adapted for residential purposes`

GIVEN `the land` IS A `The land and its use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is residential land or a strata lot used only as a home` MEANS
        `it is a residential building or a strata lot` `the land`
    AND (    (NOT (`the land`'s `there is a residential occupancy other than the owner's`))
          OR (     `the land`'s `that occupancy is one excluded residential occupancy`
               AND (`the land`'s `number of lots` LESS THAN 2 OR `the land`'s `that occupancy is on a lot the owner also lives on`)))
    AND (NOT (`the land`'s `the land is used for another purpose or earns other income`))

GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home at the taxing date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is land of a kind clause 2(1) exempts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the home`'s `the use`
    WHEN `the owner lives there` `continuously` `satisfied` THEN `it is residential land or a strata lot used only as a home` (`the home`'s `the land`)
    WHEN `the owner is building a home there` `b` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `it is a residential building or a strata lot` (`the home`'s `the land`)

-- cl 13 and cl 14.
GIVEN `the land` IS A `The land and its use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the lots meet clause 13 or 14` MEANS
       `the land`'s `number of lots` LESS THAN 2
    OR (`the land`'s `the lots adjoin` AND `the land`'s `the lots are in the same ownership` AND `the land`'s `the lots are a single residence`)

GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home at the taxing date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 11 excludes it` MEANS
       `the home`'s `a company owns or co-owns it, other than a trustee company or a trustee of a concessional trust`
    OR `the home`'s `the owners who live there are owners only as trustees`
    OR `the home`'s `a trustee of a special trust owns or co-owns it`

-- cl 12(2), (5). Under cl 12(10) the former and new residences of clause 7 count as one: for a clause 7 case, "another
-- residence" is one other than those two.
GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home at the taxing date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is the family's principal place of residence under clause 12` MEANS
       (NOT (`the home`'s `the family owns another residence one of them uses as a principal place of residence`))
    OR (IF `the home`'s `the family lodged an election in time`
        THEN `the home`'s `the family elected this residence`
        ELSE `the home`'s `this residence has the highest land value of the family's residences`)

-- cl 15 with Schedule 2 cl 70.
GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home at the taxing date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 15 is met` MEANS
       `the home`'s `percentage owned by the owners who live there` AT LEAST 25
    OR `the home`'s `the owner is a participant in an approved shared equity scheme`
    OR (`the home`'s `the owner was previously entitled to the exemption for this land` AND `the home`'s `land tax year` AT MOST 2025)

GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home at the taxing date`
GIVETH AN `Exemption answer`
`the principal place of residence exemption for` MEANS
    IF NOT (`it is used and occupied as the owner's principal place of residence` `the home`)
    THEN `not exempt` `the owner does not use and occupy it as principal place of residence, actually or under clauses 6 to 9`
    ELSE IF NOT (`it is land of a kind clause 2(1) exempts` `the home`)
         THEN `not exempt` `it is not a parcel of residential land or a strata lot`
         ELSE IF NOT (`the lots meet clause 13 or 14` (`the home`'s `the land`))
              THEN `not exempt` `it is 2 or more lots that do not meet clause 13 or 14`
              ELSE IF `clause 11 excludes it` `the home`
                   THEN `not exempt` `clause 11 excludes land owned by a company or a trustee`
                   ELSE IF NOT (`it is the family's principal place of residence under clause 12` `the home`)
                        THEN `not exempt` `another residence is the family's principal place of residence under clause 12`
                        ELSE IF NOT (`clause 15 is met` `the home`)
                             THEN `not exempt` `the owners who live there own less than a 25 percent interest`
                             ELSE `exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`

§§ `s 12 -- the land tax return`

-- s 12(1): "The Chief Commissioner may by order published in the Gazette require all persons or specified classes of
-- persons to furnish land tax returns for a specified year or years". Whether such an order covers the owner is a FACT.
-- s 12(1A): "Every person subject to such a requirement in force in respect of a year shall furnish a land tax return to
-- the Chief Commissioner on or before 31 January in that year."
-- s 12(1B): the return "must (a) set out a full and complete statement of all land owned by the person at midnight on 31
-- December in the previous year, and (b) set out, or be accompanied by, any information ... (i) the person's land
-- ownership, (ii) the eligibility of the land for an exemption from land tax or for a reduction in the taxable value".
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 12(1A) return date for` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 1 `the land tax year`

§§ `ss 39 and 40 -- when to pay, and the early payment discount`

-- s 39(1): "Land tax payable by a taxpayer is due and payable as required by the relevant notice of assessment served on
-- the taxpayer concerned." (3): "No payment of land tax is required earlier than 30 days after service of the notice of
-- assessment on the taxpayer."
`the s 39(3) days` MEANS 30

GIVEN `days from service to the due date in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from service to the day land tax must be paid` MEANS
    `the greater of` `days from service to the due date in the notice` `and` `the s 39(3) days`

-- s 40(1): "A person who pays land tax within 30 days after service of the notice of assessment of the land tax is
-- entitled to a discount of the amount of land tax specified in the assessment excluding overdue land tax if (a) the whole
-- of the amount specified in the assessment is paid, and (b) no other liability in relation to land tax, interest or
-- penalty tax is, at the time of payment, payable by the person to the Chief Commissioner (including a liability subject
-- to objection, appeal or other dispute) or any such liability is paid in full when making the payment."
-- (2): "The discount is to be at the rate determined by order of the Treasurer published in the Gazette." The rate is an
-- INPUT (the order is not deposited).
`the s 40 days` MEANS 30

GIVEN `days from service to payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole amount specified in the assessment was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no other land tax, interest or penalty tax was payable, or it was paid in full with this payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 40 discount is earned` MEANS
        `days from service to payment` AT MOST `the s 40 days`
    AND `the whole amount specified in the assessment was paid`
    AND `no other land tax, interest or penalty tax was payable, or it was paid in full with this payment`

GIVEN `the land tax specified in the assessment, excluding overdue land tax` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate ordered by the Treasurer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 40 discount on` MEANS
    `the land tax specified in the assessment, excluding overdue land tax` TIMES `the rate ordered by the Treasurer`

§§ `Land Tax Act ss 5A and 5B -- surcharge land tax on residential land owned by a foreign person`

-- s 2A: "foreign person" and "residential land" have "the same meaning as in Chapter 2A of the Duties Act 1997" -- FACTS
-- here (the Duties Act is deposited at ../../../duties-act-1997/ but not encoded with this Act).
-- s 5A(1): "Land tax is payable under this section in respect of residential land owned by a foreign person (surcharge
-- land tax)."
-- s 5A(2): on "all the residential land owned by the foreign person at midnight on 31 December in any year (commencing
-- with 2016)", for "the period of 12 months commencing on 1 January in the next succeeding year" at "(a) ... midnight on 31
-- December 2016 -- 0.75% ..., (b) ... in the years 2017-2021 -- 2% ..., (c) ... in the years 2022 and 2023 -- 4% ..., (d)
-- ... in any other year, commencing with 2024 -- 5% of that taxable value". The years named are the years of the 31 December
-- ownership date, so (FINDING 2) the land tax years are 2017 (0.75%), 2018-2022 (2%), 2023-2024 (4%) and 2025 onward (5%).
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 5A(2) surcharge rate for` MEANS
    IF `the land tax year` AT LEAST 2025
    THEN 5%
    ELSE IF `the land tax year` AT LEAST 2023
         THEN 4%
         ELSE IF `the land tax year` AT LEAST 2018
              THEN 2%
              ELSE IF `the land tax year` EQUALS 2017
                   THEN 0.75%
                   ELSE 0

-- s 5A(3): surcharge land tax "is payable in addition to any land tax payable in respect of the residential land under the
-- other provisions of this Act, and is so payable even if no land tax is payable under those other provisions".
-- s 5A(4): "(a) surcharge land tax is payable as if the residential land were the only land owned by the foreign person,
-- (b) if the residential land is also owned by a person who is not a foreign person, the taxable value of the land is to
-- be reduced to the proportionate value of the interest in the land of the foreign person, (c) if the foreign person is a
-- joint owner of the residential land, the person is to be individually (and not jointly) assessed ... in respect of the
-- value of the person's proportionate interest", "(d) if the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that the residential land is
-- used for purposes other than residential purposes, the taxable value of the land is to be reduced by the apportionment
-- factor determined in accordance with section 104ZB of the Duties Act 1997" (not covered), "(h) the tax thresholds under
-- Division 4A of Part 7 of the Principal Act do not apply to surcharge land tax" (FINDING 3: Division 4A is repealed; the
-- thresholds are in Division 4), "(i) any other modification prescribed by the regulations ... applies" (FINDING 8).
-- The taxable value is the total of the person's proportionate interests in the average values (s 9) of the residential
-- land, leaving out land exempt from surcharge.
DECLARE `Residential land of a foreign person` HAS
    `land tax year`                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the owner is a foreign person`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of the owner's interests in residential land not exempt from surcharge` IS A NUMBER
    `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied some of it is used for other than residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the land` IS A `Residential land of a foreign person`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the surcharge land tax on` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the land`'s `the owner is a foreign person`)
    THEN `answered` 0
    ELSE IF `the land`'s `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied some of it is used for other than residential purposes`
         THEN `not covered` `residential land partly used for other purposes needs the Duties Act 1997 s 104ZB apportionment factor, not deposited`
         ELSE `answered` (`the land`'s `the value of the owner's interests in residential land not exempt from surcharge` TIMES `the s 5A(2) surcharge rate for` (`the land`'s `land tax year`))

-- s 5A(4)(g): the foreign person "is exempt from liability to pay surcharge land tax in respect of the land for a land tax
-- year because the land is the principal place of residence of the foreign person ... only if the person is eligible for
-- the exemption under section 5B".
-- s 5B(1): "A person is eligible ... only if (a) the person is a permanent resident at midnight on 31 December of the
-- previous year, and (b) the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that, during the land tax year, the person intends to use and
-- occupy the land as the principal place of residence of the person in accordance with the residence requirement, and (c)
-- the person lodges a declaration with a land tax return required to be furnished under section 12 of the Principal Act
-- for the land tax year to the effect that the person has that intention." (FINDING 9: the declaration rides on a return
-- that s 12 requires.)
-- s 5BA(1): s 5B applies to a retirement visa holder "subject to any modifications prescribed by the regulations" (not
-- deposited: not covered).
DECLARE `Surcharge home facts` HAS
    `the home is exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was a permanent resident at midnight on 31 December of the previous year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the person intends to meet the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person lodged the declaration with a land tax return required under s 12` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a retirement visa holder`                                IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Surcharge home facts`
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`the s 5B(1) eligibility of` MEANS
    IF `the facts`'s `the person is a retirement visa holder`
    THEN `not covered` `the answer depends on the Land Tax Management Regulation 2024, which is not deposited`
    ELSE `answered` (    `the facts`'s `the home is exempt under the principal place of residence exemption`
                     AND `the facts`'s `the person was a permanent resident at midnight on 31 December of the previous year`
                     AND `the facts`'s `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the person intends to meet the residence requirement`
                     AND `the facts`'s `the person lodged the declaration with a land tax return required under s 12`)

-- s 5B(2): "The person must use and occupy the land as the person's principal place of residence for a continuous period
-- of 200 days in the land tax year. This requirement is referred to as the residence requirement." (2A): "A person does
-- not use and occupy land as the person's principal place of residence during a period of the person's physical absence
-- from Australia." (2B): the Chief Commissioner may waive (2A) for a brief absence "in exceptional circumstances" (an
-- input: a waived absence does not break the stretch).
`the s 5B(2) days` MEANS 200

GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest day to begin the s 5B(2) period in` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 `the land tax year`) MINUS (`the s 5B(2) days` MINUS 1))

-- A stretch of continuous use and occupation, both days counted; only the part inside the land tax year counts.
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER, `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of the stretch in the land tax year` MEANS
    `the greater of` ((`the last counted` MINUS `the first counted`) PLUS 1) `and` 0
    WHERE
        `the first counted` MEANS `the greater of` (DATE_SERIAL `the first day`) `and` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 `the land tax year`))
        `the last counted` MEANS `the lesser of` (DATE_SERIAL `the last day`) `and` (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 `the land tax year`))

GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER, `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the residence requirement is met by` MEANS
    `the days of the stretch in the land tax year` `the land tax year` `the first day` `the last day` AT LEAST `the s 5B(2) days`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the owner, the taxpayer, the family, the foreign person and the Chief Commissioner`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day each rule names.
DECLARE `Land tax party` IS ONE OF
    `the owner`
    `the taxpayer`
    `the members of the family`
    `the foreign person`
    `the Chief Commissioner`

DECLARE `Land tax act` IS ONE OF
    `furnish a land tax return setting out all land owned at midnight on 31 December`
    `lodge a written election of the family's principal place of residence`
    `treat the elected residence as the family's principal place of residence`
    `treat the residence with the highest land value as the family's principal place of residence`
    `begin actually using and occupying the land as principal place of residence`
    `stop using and occupying the land as principal place of residence`
    `begin actually using and occupying the new residence as principal place of residence`
    `pay the land tax assessed`
    `pay the whole amount specified in the assessment`
    `allow the early payment discount`
    `complete 200 days of continuous use and occupation as principal place of residence`

-- s 12(1A)-(1B). Clock: day 0 is 1 January of the land tax year; 31 January is day 30.
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from 1 January to the s 12(1A) return date` MEANS
    `days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 `the land tax year`) `to` (`the s 12(1A) return date for` `the land tax year`)

GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
      `a Gazette order under s 12(1) requires the owner to furnish a return for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
DECIDE `s 12(1A)-(1B) -- a person a Gazette order covers must lodge a land tax return by 31 January` IS
    IF `a Gazette order under s 12(1) requires the owner to furnish a return for the year`
    THEN PARTY `the owner`
         MUST  `furnish a land tax return setting out all land owned at midnight on 31 December`
         WITHIN `days from 1 January to the s 12(1A) return date` `the land tax year`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "s 12(1A)-(1B): a person subject to a Gazette order under s 12(1) must furnish, on or before 31 January, a land tax return setting out all land owned at midnight on the previous 31 December"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Schedule 1A cl 12(3): the election "is to be made, by or on behalf of the members of the family, in writing and must be
-- lodged with the Chief Commissioner within the period for the lodging of objections under section 89 of the Taxation
-- Administration Act 1996". (4): "by the end of the period allowed for the lodging of an objection to a notice of
-- assessment of land tax liability (being an initial assessment of land tax liability) for that tax year". (2): the Chief
-- Commissioner "is to treat the one place of residence elected"; (5): "If an election is not made, the Chief Commissioner
-- is to treat the residence that has the highest land value". The objection period is set by the Taxation Administration
-- Act 1996 s 89, NOT DEPOSITED: an INPUT. Electing is a choice, so missing the period is no breach; it brings the cl 12(5)
-- rule into play. Clock: day 0 is the day the initial notice of assessment is served.
GIVEN `days in the s 89 objection period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
DECIDE `Schedule 1A cl 12(2)-(5) -- the family may elect its principal place of residence within the objection period` IS
    PARTY `the members of the family`
    DO    `lodge a written election of the family's principal place of residence`
    WITHIN `days in the s 89 objection period`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Chief Commissioner` MUST `treat the elected residence as the family's principal place of residence`)
    LEST  (PARTY `the Chief Commissioner` MUST `treat the residence with the highest land value as the family's principal place of residence`)

-- Schedule 1A cl 6(5): the exemption "is revoked if the person fails to actually use and occupy the land as the person's
-- principal place of residence by the end of the period in which this clause applies ... and to continue to so use and
-- occupy the land for at least 6 months". (6): "the principal place of residence exemption is taken not to have applied to
-- the land in respect of any tax year to which, but for the revocation, it would have applied. Land tax liability is to
-- be assessed or reassessed accordingly." Clock: day 0 is any day the caller picks; the caller gives the days to the end of
-- the clause 6 period, and the days in the 6 months after the day the owner moves in.
GIVEN `days to the end of the clause 6 period` IS A NUMBER
      `days in the 6 months after the owner moves in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
DECIDE `Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6) -- to keep the building exemption the owner must move in by the end of the period and stay 6 months` IS
    PARTY `the owner`
    MUST  `begin actually using and occupying the land as principal place of residence`
    WITHIN `days to the end of the clause 6 period`
    HENCE
        PARTY `the owner`
        SHANT `stop using and occupying the land as principal place of residence`
        WITHIN (`days in the 6 months after the owner moves in` MINUS 1)
        LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6): the owner did not keep living there for 6 months; the exemption is revoked and every tax year it covered is reassessed"
    LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "Schedule 1A cl 6(5)-(6): the owner did not move in by the end of the clause 6 period; the exemption is revoked and every tax year it covered is reassessed"

-- Schedule 1A cl 7(3A): the exemption that applied by operation of clause 7 to land not actually used and occupied by the
-- person at the relevant taxing date "is revoked if the person is not actually using and occupying the new residence as
-- the person's principal place of residence by the next taxing date immediately following the relevant taxing date". (4):
-- the exemption "is taken not to have applied in respect of the tax year ... Land tax liability is to be assessed or
-- reassessed accordingly." Clock: day 0 is the relevant taxing date.
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from the taxing date to the next taxing date for` MEANS
    `days from` (`the taxing date for` `the land tax year`) `to` (`the next taxing date after the one for` `the land tax year`)

GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
DECIDE `Schedule 1A cl 7(3A)-(4) -- to keep both exemptions the owner must be living in the new residence by the next taxing date` IS
    PARTY `the owner`
    MUST  `begin actually using and occupying the new residence as principal place of residence`
    WITHIN `days from the taxing date to the next taxing date for` `the land tax year`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "Schedule 1A cl 7(3A)-(4): the owner was not living in the new residence by the next taxing date; the clause 7 exemption is revoked and that tax year is reassessed"

-- s 39(1), (3). Clock: day 0 is the day the notice of assessment is served.
GIVEN `days from service to the due date in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
DECIDE `s 39(1), (3) -- the taxpayer must pay by the due date in the notice, which is not earlier than 30 days after service` IS
    PARTY `the taxpayer`
    MUST  `pay the land tax assessed`
    WITHIN `days from service to the day land tax must be paid` `days from service to the due date in the notice`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "s 39(1), (3): land tax is due as the notice of assessment requires, and not earlier than 30 days after service; interest and penalty tax on late payment are under the Taxation Administration Act 1996 (not deposited)"

-- s 40(1). Paying early is a choice: not paying within 30 days is no breach, it only forgoes the discount. Clock: day 0 is
-- the day the notice of assessment is served.
GIVEN `no other land tax, interest or penalty tax is payable, or it is paid in full with this payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
DECIDE `s 40 -- paying the whole amount within 30 days of service earns the discount` IS
    IF `no other land tax, interest or penalty tax is payable, or it is paid in full with this payment`
    THEN PARTY `the taxpayer`
         DO    `pay the whole amount specified in the assessment`
         WITHIN `the s 40 days`
         HENCE (PARTY `the Chief Commissioner` MUST `allow the early payment discount`)
         LEST  FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(4). (3): "If the residence requirement is not complied with by the person, surcharge land tax
-- liability is to be assessed or reassessed as if the person's exemption from liability to pay surcharge land tax for the
-- land tax year had never applied." (4): "The failure of the person to comply with the residence requirement is taken to
-- be a tax default for the purposes of Part 5 of the Taxation Administration Act 1996." The event is the day the 200th
-- continuous day is completed. Clock: day 0 is 1 January of the land tax year.
GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from 1 January to 31 December of` MEANS
    `days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 `the land tax year`) `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 `the land tax year`)

GIVEN `the land tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
DECIDE `Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(4) -- a foreign person exempt from surcharge on the home must live there 200 continuous days in the year` IS
    PARTY `the foreign person`
    MUST  `complete 200 days of continuous use and occupation as principal place of residence`
    WITHIN `days from 1 January to 31 December of` `the land tax year`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the foreign person` BECAUSE "Land Tax Act s 5B(2)-(4): the residence requirement was not met; surcharge land tax is assessed or reassessed as if the exemption had never applied, and the failure is a tax default under Part 5 of the Taxation Administration Act 1996"
